inister-gadkari/articleshow/135485146.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nhai-to-use-desilted-river-material-for-road-projects-in-bihar-says-transport-minister-gadkari/articleshow/135485146.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-03T12:21:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135485550,imgsize-63560.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dilip Ghosh takes 'Sonia' jibe at Mamata for joining INDIA bloc rally against SIR]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dilip-ghosh-takes-sonia-jibe-at-mamata-for-joining-india-bloc-rally-against-sir/articleshow/135485381.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135485381.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Dilip Ghosh has publicly lambasted Mamata Banerjee for her involvement in the INDIA bloc rally concerning changes to the electoral roll. He argues her party's diminishing political clout is prompting her to seek validation through an alliance with Congress. Ghosh highlighted her past victories, labeling her claims regarding electoral integrity as hypocritical, and pointed out the positive impact of removing fraudulent voters in fostering fair elections in West Bengal.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dilip-ghosh-takes-sonia-jibe-at-mamata-for-joining-india-bloc-rally-against-sir/articleshow/135485381.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dilip-ghosh-takes-sonia-jibe-at-mamata-for-joining-india-bloc-rally-against-sir/articleshow/135485381.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-03T12:07:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135485734,imgsize-71828.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Targeting civilian infrastructure must end': MEA after Indian national killed in attack on ship in Oman]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/targeting-civilian-infrastructure-must-end-mea-after-indian-national-killed-in-attack-on-ship-in-oman/articleshow/135485434.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135485434.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/targeting-civilian-infrastructure-must-end-mea-after-indian-national-killed-in-attack-on-ship-in-oman/articleshow/135485434.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/targeting-civilian-infrastructure-must-end-mea-after-indian-national-killed-in-attack-on-ship-in-oman/articleshow/135485434.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-03T12:04:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135485577,imgsize-39704.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Rs 25cr spent on ads to claim no stubble burning, FIRs tell another story': BJP targets AAP govt in Punjab]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rs-25cr-spent-on-ads-to-claim-no-stubble-burning-firs-tell-another-story-bjp-targets-aap-govt-in-punjab/articleshow/135483258.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135483258.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Delhi Environment Minister Manjinder Singh Sirsa accused the Punjab government of permitting stubble burning while contradicting its claims. He alleged that Punjab's government had registered FIRs against farmers involved in stubble burning activities. Sirsa criticized the appointment of Reena Gupta as chairperson of the Punjab Pollution Control Board as an attempt to manipulate pollution data. He emphasized the adverse impact of Punjab's stubble burning on Delhi's air quality.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rs-25cr-spent-on-ads-to-claim-no-stubble-burning-firs-tell-another-story-bjp-targets-aap-govt-in-punjab/articleshow/135483258.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rs-25cr-spent-on-ads-to-claim-no-stubble-burning-firs-tell-another-story-bjp-targets-aap-govt-in-punjab/articleshow/135483258.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-03T12:01:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135485436,imgsize-82568.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Doesn’t have courage to call all-party meet?’: Congress questions Shah over delay in discussion on delimitation Bill]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/doesnt-have-courage-to-call-all-party-meet-congress-questions-shah-over-delay-in-discussion-on-delimitation-bill/articleshow/135483878.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135483878.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/doesnt-have-courage-to-call-all-party-meet-congress-questions-shah-over-delay-in-discussion-on-delimitation-bill/articleshow/135483878.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/doesnt-have-courage-to-call-all-party-meet-congress-questions-shah-over-delay-in-discussion-on-delimitation-bill/articleshow/135483878.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-03T11:26:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135484369,imgsize-119288.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1 killed, 13 rescued after unidentified aerial object strikes Indian vessel near Oman]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/1-killed-13-rescued-after-unidentified-aerial-object-strikes-indian-vessel-near-oman/articleshow/135483233.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135483233.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[An Indian seafarer from Gujarat was killed after an unidentified aerial object struck the Indian-flagged vessel MSV AL JUSUFI off the Oman coast on Monday. The remaining 13 crew members were rescued by the Omani Coast Guard. Union minister Sarbananda Sonowal said Indian authorities were coordinating with Oman to assist the survivors and arrange their repatriation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/1-killed-13-rescued-after-unidentified-aerial-object-strikes-indian-vessel-near-oman/articleshow/135483233.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/1-killed-13-rescued-after-unidentified-aerial-object-strikes-indian-vessel-near-oman/articleshow/135483233.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-03T10:47:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135483477,imgsize-818641.cms"/></item></channel></rss>